# .loom/resync-ignore — paths Loom must not overwrite or delete on resync.
#
# See .loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md for the full rule. Each entry below
# pins a deliberate, repo-specific divergence from the upstream rjwalters/loom
# defaults/ tree — a fix landed directly in this repo's installed copy
# because it was not (yet) upstreamed.

# #5552: restores the isDraft/exit-13 draft-PR exclusion from PR #5543
# (commit 0560777c), which a routine "chore: resync installed Loom surfaces"
# pass (4b4523e4) silently reverted ~2.5 hours after it merged, because the
# fix was a direct edit to the vendored copy rather than an upstream change.
# Pin these four paths so a future resync is blocked-and-explicit (or
# skipped once pinned) instead of silently reverting the fix a second time.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
#
# NOTE: entries use the ".loom/"-relative report form (per the convention
# documented in resync-installed.sh's header comment), NOT the repo-relative
# spelling, for the .claude/commands/loom/ entry below — is_ignored()'s
# fallback normalization only strips a leading "./" and ".loom/", so
# ".claude/commands/loom/judge.md" would NOT match the "commands/loom/judge.md"
# rel it is compared against; only the unprefixed form does.
scripts/judge-fallback-guard.sh
scripts/tests/test-judge-fallback-cap.sh
commands/loom/judge.md
roles/judge.md

# #5690: a `Part of #N` trailer written inside an inline code span is
# deliberately NOT read as a declaration (#5234's code-span exclusion, which is
# correct and unchanged here), so merge-pr.sh's partial-increment
# `loom:building` -> `loom:issue` reset (#3667) silently no-ops — the incident
# on PR #5686 / issue #5240. Two local fixes, neither of which touches the
# loom-daemon parser: a non-blocking pre-merge warning in merge-pr.sh
# (_warn_backticked_partial_increment_trailers + its two text helpers, with
# regression cases in the partial-increment suite) and a plain-text-not-
# backticked caution next to the trailer example in builder-pr.md (both
# installed copies, which must stay byte-identical).
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
scripts/merge-pr.sh
scripts/tests/test-merge-pr-partial-increment.sh
commands/loom/builder-pr.md
roles/builder-pr.md
